Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='prodromechain', at=datetime(2026, 8, 31, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="Prodrome is the todo system's own VCS: a content-addressed Merkle DAG of events, with no tree object", body='*Prodrome* (`events/`): the todo system\'s own VCS — a content-addressed Merkle chain of lifecycle events, one canonical constructor-literal per object (PARSED by a whitelist walker, never imported/eval\'d), byte-hash verification (shipped kinds\' fields are frozen; evolution adds kinds), fold = function of the event SET (merge-convergent). Triage-actor events are provisional by construction; git is transport + second witness, not the truth. Genesis backfilled 2026-08-31 from 229 commits (165 events since Oct 2025). Since the inversion (0.10, 2026-09-01) the chain holds todo CONTENT (`Authored`). *A log that is a DAG* (2026-09-04; "order is causal, time is data"): `Woven(parents, event)`, with `event=None` for a plain merge (a merge is structure, not a fact about a todo), and since 2026-09-30 `Change(genesis, deps, event)`, whose deps are its todo\'s heads, what its writer saw (SPEC §3, since 2026-10-01), the only object written since 2026-10-03 besides an empty store\'s `Genesis` (above, Limits); the legacy `Sealed` and `Woven` are read, never written. Still NO tree object (REJECTED: a derived index kept consistent by hand is the dual-write class the inversion killed). `verify` reports an untrusted event dated behind ANY ancestor (the agent\'s `at` is the server clock, so that is a forged object or a clock gone backwards).', rationale='Genesis backfilled 2026-08-31 from 229 commits (165 events since Oct 2025); content since the inversion (0.10, 2026-09-01); a DAG since 2026-09-04; Change since 2026-09-30. A tree object was rejected: a derived index kept consistent by hand is the dual-write class the inversion killed.', supersedes=()))